#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"Automatic erasure under rule %(rule)s. The approval is the rule itself, "
"approved when the retention term was decided; there is no case-by-case "
"approval, the erasure bearing on three fields and not being triggered by a "
"person. The account named as having destroyed and approved is the one the "
"watcher runs under."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:ir.model,name:bf_route_privacy.model_privacy_document_classification
msgid "Classification documentaire (RP)"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:ir.model,name:bf_route_privacy.model_res_company
msgid "Companies"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:privacy.purpose,name:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_place_from_position
msgid "Customer's place proposed from a position read"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid "Fields set back to zero: %s."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_place_from_position
msgid ""
"It is a proposal: someone on the team accepts or refuses it,\n"
"                and nothing is written without that acceptance. A reading that\n"
"                is too imprecise is not proposed at all."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:privacy.purpose,name:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_road_measured
msgid "Kilometres of a day measured from the positions read"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"Latitude, longitude and accuracy in metres of the person on the road, read "
"once at the moment they marked the stop."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"Not covered, and still held: the stop itself, its arrival time, its marking "
"time, the person who marked it, their note and the time on site, which are "
"the proof of the visit and follow the project file; the position notice as "
"it was read (bf.route.notice.ack), which is the proof of the prior "
"information of s. 8.1 and must outlive the position it made lawful; the "
"kilometres of the day measured from the readings before they were erased, "
"which is a distance and not a place and which falls under rule ROU-002, six "
"years; and, where an office person accepted one of these readings as a "
"customer's place on the map, that copy, which has become the customer's own "
"address and carries on the contact the date it was accepted."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:privacy.purpose,name:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_position
msgid "Position read at the stops of a route"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"Position read on the phone on %(marked)s, at the \"%(customer)s\" stop of "
"the day \"%(day)s\", erased at the end of the company's %(days)s day(s) of "
"retention."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/res_company.py:0
msgid ""
"Positions cannot be read: the privacy register declares no retention term for them. Its retention policy is missing, archived, or set to zero days.\n"
"\n"
"Declare the term first. Each erasure is sealed in the destruction register as an immutable entry citing that rule, and a processing nobody declared is one nobody can object to."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"Section 23 of Quebec's Law 25: personal information is destroyed when the "
"purpose for which it was collected is accomplished. The purpose is proving "
"the visit and settling a disagreement about a delivery. Section 8.1: the "
"person had been informed beforehand of the reading and of the means offered "
"to activate it. Section 3.2: framework for retention and destruction."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model:ir.model,name:bf_route_privacy.model_bf_route_day_stop
msgid "Stop of a route day"
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_position
msgid ""
"The position is erased at the end of the retention calendar.\n"
"                The stop, its time and your mark remain: they are what proves\n"
"                the visit."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/res_company.py:0
msgid ""
"The privacy register declares that positions read on a route are kept at most %(declared)s (purpose \"%(rule)s\", rule ROU-001), and %(company)s is set to keep them %(applied)s.\n"
"\n"
"Lower the setting, or declare the longer term in the register. Keeping them for LESS is fine and needs nothing: section 23 of Law 25 asks that information be destroyed once its purpose is accomplished, which is a ceiling, and each erasure names the term it actually applied."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"The register refuses to attest the erasure of the position at the stop of "
"\"%(stop)s\": %(fields)s still hold a value. Nothing was recorded and the "
"erasure is undone; bf_route's purge will come back on its next pass."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#. odoo-python
#: code:addons/bf_route_privacy/models/bf_route_day_stop.py:0
msgid ""
"The register refuses to attest the erasure of the position at the stop of "
"\"%(stop)s\": the \"position erased\" mark is not set, so nothing on the "
"record says a position ever existed."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_road_measured
msgid ""
"The road between the positions read at your stops is\n"
"                measured, in the order you marked them, and kept on the day as\n"
"                a number of kilometres, beside the odometer readings."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_road_measured
msgid ""
"This number is a distance, not a place: it says how far the\n"
"                day drove, not where it went. It stays on the day after the\n"
"                positions themselves have been erased, and it is kept six years\n"
"                under rule ROU-002, the term the tax law sets for books and\n"
"                records."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_place_from_position
msgid ""
"What is kept in the end is the customer's place, not the\n"
"                position of the person who marked the stop. But that copy stays\n"
"                with the customer: it has become their address, and it is not\n"
"                erased with the position it came from. The customer's record\n"
"                carries the date it was accepted."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_road_measured
msgid ""
"What it is for: comparing the kilometres claimed with the\n"
"                road actually driven, in the register the company keeps for its\n"
"                vehicles. It is never added into the odometer's total."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_position
msgid ""
"What it is for: proving the visit to the customer, settling a\n"
"                disagreement about a delivery, and measuring the kilometres of\n"
"                the day. Who sees it: the people who manage the routes, and you,\n"
"                on your own stops."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_place_from_position
msgid ""
"When a customer's record has no coordinates and their address\n"
"                could not be found automatically, the position read at their\n"
"                stop can be proposed as their place on the map."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_position
msgid ""
"When you mark a stop on your route (done, customer absent,\n"
"                postponed), the application reads your phone's position\n"
"                <b>once</b>, at that moment, and keeps it with the stop as proof\n"
"                of the visit. It does not follow you between stops, nor before\n"
"                the day starts, nor after it ends."
msgstr ""

#. module: bf_route_privacy
#: model_terms:privacy.purpose,plain_language_summary:bf_route_privacy.purpose_route_position
msgid ""
"Your phone asks for your permission the first time. If you\n"
"                refuse, the stops are marked without a position, and your\n"
"                refusal is not recorded."
msgstr ""

